---
title: Remizidae
---
# Remizidae

Remizidae is a small Old World family of tiny, tit-like songbirds, of which the
[[penduline-tit]] is the best known. The males plait and felt a thick-walled
purse for the eggs out of plant down and spider silk, and sling it from a
drooping twig so that it swings free with nothing supporting it from below —
among the most elaborate structures any songbird makes. The family is not
closely related to the true tits despite the resemblance.
